// This file exists purely for FFI support into contracts.
// Any types that are not C-native but must be passed into wasm contracts (at e.g. syscall boundaries)
// are defined here; then, cbindgen generates corresponding definitions for those types.
// Note that the XDR types generated by x23c do NOT necessarily have the same layout as those generated by rust.
// Discriminated unions (specifically with repr(i32)) have a well-defined layout,
// but one that is not the same as the common tagged union layout which x23c uses for the generated C++ types.
// x23c also makes no explicit guarantees about the generated layouts; so we prefer to regenerate the types
// here using cbindgen, so that there is no possibility of mismatch between the generated types.

// This file is intended to be empty.
